summary: A painter who works with visual artists on the gap between "I should paint today" and actually picking up a brush.
+++

Priya spent a decade painting professionally before she started coaching
other visual artists through the exact block she used to fight herself:
the studio door that somehow never gets opened.

Her approach leans heavily on practice structure over inspiration —
showing up on a schedule small enough to actually keep, and treating a
bad session as data rather than a verdict.

Certified in creative coaching since 2021; work has shown in three
regional galleries.
